description:
Implement the /events/<slug> detail view and /o/<slug> organizer profile view. Replaces stubs left by bead 1. Depends on bead 1 (kb-csd.1) for routing and bead 2 (kb-csd.2) because both beads share /workspace/events/views.py — bead 3 must apply its changes on top of bead 2's final event_list implementation.

Design doc section: '/events/<slug> detail', '/o/<slug> organizer profile'

## Files to create/modify

- /workspace/events/views.py (MODIFY — replace event_detail stub; event_list from bead 2 must be preserved)
- /workspace/templates/events/detail.html (NEW — directory /workspace/templates/events/ was created in bead 2)
- /workspace/organizers/views.py (REPLACE stub with real organizer_profile view)
- /workspace/templates/organizers/profile.html (NEW — create directory first: mkdir -p /workspace/templates/organizers)
- /workspace/templates/cotton/organizer_mini_card.html (NEW)

## events/views.py — replace event_detail stub

After bead 2, /workspace/events/views.py has event_list fully implemented AND already imports
get_object_or_404 (bead 2 includes it in the import to avoid the bead 3 agent needing to add it).

The import line at the top of the file after bead 2 is already:
  from django.shortcuts import get_object_or_404, render

No import change is needed. Simply replace the event_detail stub function with:

```python
def event_detail(request, slug):
    event = get_object_or_404(
        Event.objects.select_related("organizer", "venue")
        .prefetch_related("tags", "images"),
        slug=slug,
        status="published",
    )
    cover_image = event.images.filter(is_cover=True).first()
    context = {
        "event": event,
        "cover_image": cover_image,
    }
    return render(request, "events/detail.html", context)
```

Notes:
- Event.slug is unique per organizer (UniqueConstraint on organizer+slug), NOT globally unique.
  If two organizers share a slug, get_object_or_404 may raise MultipleObjectsReturned.
  For phase 0.3 internal use this is an acceptable known limitation.
- EventImage related_name="images" is confirmed in /workspace/events/models.py line 114.
- get_object_or_404 on status="published" means draft/review events return 404 (correct).

## organizers/views.py — replace stub

The file at /workspace/organizers/views.py after bead 1 is a stub. Replace the entire file:

```python
from django.shortcuts import get_object_or_404, render
from django.utils import timezone

from events.models import Event

from .models import Organizer


def organizer_profile(request, slug):
    organizer = get_object_or_404(Organizer, slug=slug, status="approved")
    now = timezone.now()

    upcoming_events = (
        Event.objects.filter(
            organizer=organizer,
            status="published",
            start__gte=now,
        )
        .select_related("venue")
        .prefetch_related("tags")
        .order_by("start")
    )
    past_events = (
        Event.objects.filter(
            organizer=organizer,
            status="published",
            start__lt=now,
        )
        .select_related("venue")
        .prefetch_related("tags")
        .order_by("-start")[:20]
    )

    context = {
        "organizer": organizer,
        "upcoming_events": upcoming_events,
        "past_events": past_events,
    }
    return render(request, "organizers/profile.html", context)
```

Notes:
- get_object_or_404 on status="approved" means candidate/suspended organizers return 404.
- Past events capped at 20 most recent.
- Organizer.slug is globally unique (confirmed in /workspace/organizers/models.py line 9).

## Confirmed model fields (from /workspace/organizers/models.py and /workspace/venues/models.py)

Organizer fields: name, slug, description, avatar (ImageField), website, telegram_channel,
  status (candidate/approved/suspended), verified_badge (BooleanField).
Venue fields: name, slug, neighborhood (CharField, blank=True), address, latitude, longitude.

## templates/events/detail.html

Directory /workspace/templates/events/ was created in bead 2.

```html
{% extends "_base.html" %}
{% load i18n %}

{% block title %}{{ event.title }} — Kinky Bubbles{% endblock %}

{% block layout %}
<article class="max-w-2xl mx-auto flex flex-col gap-6">

  {% if cover_image %}
  <img src="{{ cover_image.image.url }}"
       alt="{{ cover_image.alt|default:event.title }}"
       class="w-full rounded-xl object-cover max-h-64">
  {% endif %}

  <header class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">{{ event.title }}</h1>
    {% if event.organizer %}
      <c-organizer-mini-card :organizer="event.organizer" />
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm">
    <p><span class="font-semibold">{% trans "Date" %}:</span> {{ event.start|date:"D, d M Y" }}</p>
    <p>
      <span class="font-semibold">{% trans "Time" %}:</span>
      {{ event.start|date:"H:i" }}{% if event.end %} – {{ event.end|date:"H:i" }}{% endif %}
    </p>
    {% if event.venue %}
    <p>
      <span class="font-semibold">{% trans "Venue" %}:</span>
      {{ event.venue.name }}{% if event.venue.neighborhood %}, {{ event.venue.neighborhood }}{% endif %}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
    <p>
      <span class="font-semibold">{% trans "Price" %}:</span>
      {% if event.is_free %}
        {% trans "Free" %}
      {% elif event.price_min_cents %}
        {{ event.currency }} {{ event.price_min_cents }}
        {% if event.price_max_cents %} – {{ event.price_max_cents }}{% endif %}
        {% if event.sliding_scale %} ({% trans "sliding scale" %}){% endif %}
      {% else %}
        {% trans "See event page" %}
      {% endif %}
    </p>
  </section>

  {% if event.tags.all %}
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    {% for tag in event.tags.all %}
      <a href="{% url 'event-list' %}?tags={{ tag.slug }}" class="badge badge-outline">
        {{ tag.label }}
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if event.description %}
  <section class="prose prose-sm max-w-none">
    {{ event.description|linebreaks }}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if event.tickets_url or event.external_url %}
  <div class="flex gap-3">
    {% if event.tickets_url %}
      <a href="{{ event.tickets_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
         class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">{% trans "Get tickets" %}</a>
    {% elif event.external_url %}
      <a href="{{ event.external_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
         class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">{% trans "More info" %}</a>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <footer class="text-xs text-base-content/50 border-t pt-4">
    {% trans "Safety first. Consent is mandatory. Look out for each other." %}
  </footer>

</article>
{% endblock %}
```

Note: c-organizer-mini-card receives full organizer object via `:organizer="event.organizer"`
(colon prefix passes the live Python object, not a string representation).

## templates/organizers/profile.html

Create directory first: mkdir -p /workspace/templates/organizers

```html
{% extends "_base.html" %}
{% load i18n %}

{% block title %}{{ organizer.name }} — Kinky Bubbles{% endblock %}

{% block layout %}
<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto flex flex-col gap-8">

  <header class="flex items-start gap-4">
    {% if organizer.avatar %}
    <img src="{{ organizer.avatar.url }}"
         alt="{{ organizer.name }}"
         class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full object-cover">
    {% else %}
    <div class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full bg-base-300 flex items-center justify-center text-2xl">
      {{ organizer.name|first|upper }}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
        {{ organizer.name }}
        {% if organizer.verified_badge %}
          <span class="badge badge-info badge-sm">{% trans "Verified" %}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </h1>
      {% if organizer.website %}
        <a href="{{ organizer.website }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
           class="text-sm link">{{ organizer.website }}</a>
      {% endif %}
      {% if organizer.telegram_channel %}
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">Telegram: {{ organizer.telegram_channel }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </header>

  {% if organizer.description %}
  <section class="prose prose-sm max-w-none">
    {{ organizer.description|linebreaks }}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">{% trans "Upcoming events" %}</h2>
    {% if upcoming_events %}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      {% for event in upcoming_events %}
        <c-event-card :event="event" />
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <p class="text-base-content/60">{% trans "No upcoming events." %}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  {% if past_events %}
  <details class="collapse collapse-arrow bg-base-200">
    <summary class="collapse-title text-lg font-semibold">
      {% trans "Past events" %}
    </summary>
    <div class="collapse-content flex flex-col gap-3 pt-2">
      {% for event in past_events %}
        <c-event-card :event="event" />
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </details>
  {% endif %}

</div>
{% endblock %}
```

Note: c-event-card used here via `:event="event"` — same Cotton component created in bead 2.

